### Explanation of Key Components

- **Date Logging**: Using `new Date()` ensures that every log entry includes the exact moment when the request was made.

- **File System Access**: By appending messages to a text file (`./log.txt`), you can maintain a chronological record of all HTTP requests handled by your application. This file can be accessed later for analysis or debugging purposes.

- **Error Handling**: If an error occurs while attempting to append to the log file, it will propagate up through the middleware chain until it reaches the end of the stack, at which point it will be rethrown.

