```
This code will fetch the current time and check what hour it is, then set the background image of a div element called `#sun` accordingly. The URL paths in quotes should point to images representing different times of day. You would also need to add additional cases to cover other hours of the day.
Note: This code assumes that you have already added the necessary HTTP requests to your project to connect to your weather API or database. If not, you may need to modify the PHP code to include these requests as well.
Also note that this code only updates the appearance of the sun every hour, so it won't change when the sun moves across the sky. For more advanced functionality, you may want to look into using a web service such as OpenWeatherMap or Sunrise/Sunset API which provides real-time sunrise/sunset information along with hourly temperature data.
